      <Comment source="AU4FS-4, SRI, caspi">Adenosine 5&apos;-phosphoramidate was first discovered in 1981 among cellular nucleotides purified from the green alga |FRAME:TAX-3078| |CITS: [7306093]|. While the enzyme that syntheiszes it has been characterized, knowledge of its occurrence, biochemistry and biological roles is scarce. The compound can be hydrolyzed by at least two enzymes - dinucleoside triphosphatase (|FRAME: BIS5-ADENOSYL-TRIPHOSPHATASE-RXN &quot;EC 3.6.1.29&quot;|) and |FRAME:CPLX0-7755| |CITS: [21403921]|.</Comment>
